{
  "schema": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "status",
    "description": "Report plankit configuration and repository state"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "id": "pk-status",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "pk status"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reports the resolved policy from "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the current branch and tree state, the preserved plan count, the pending plan, and the latest tag."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The tag line reads the clone. When the clone has no tags, as a fresh clone of only the working branch does in a cloud sandbox, the line says what origin has, "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "none locally; origin has v1.2.0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", read from origin without fetching; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "none yet"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " means neither has a version tag, so nothing has been released. "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk changelog"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " fetches the tags itself when it runs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The release line names the flow and what a release does. Merge flow: "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "merge flow: pk ship merges develop into main and tags it"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the branch checked out as the source; on the release branch itself the source reads "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "the working branch"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Trunk flow, when "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " sets no release branch: "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "trunk flow: pk ship tags main, origin's default branch"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The default branch comes from the clone's record of origin's default, or from origin when the clone holds none; only a repository with no origin leaves it unnamed. An empty release branch is that flow, not a gap in the policy. JSON carries it as "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "releaseFlow"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "merge"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " or "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "trunk"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The guard line ends with the protected branches, or "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "no protected branches"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " when "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "guard.branches"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is empty: then no branch is guarded against mutation, while the push guard still applies on every branch."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "usage",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Usage"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeblock",
      "lang": "bash",
      "text": "pk status\npk status --format json\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Exit code "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " means configured; "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " means not configured or not a git repository. "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--format json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " emits one object with the same fields as the text report."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "An unconfigured repository is a state, not an error: plankit is off wherever "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is absent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A configured repository whose release branch is its only branch gets a note naming the command that starts a working branch. One whose release branch does not exist gets the command that creates it at the root commit, carrying no unreleased work. In merge flow, a release branch that has moved past its last tag is noted with the number of commits not in a release. A last tag the checked-out branch does not contain, the mark of a history rewritten after a release, is noted with the way out. A pending plan, recorded by the preserve hook and not yet committed, is shown with its path and noted with its two ways out, "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "/plankit:preserve"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk preserve --discard"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "; a pointer whose plan file is gone is marked missing. One whose "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".claude/settings.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " lacks a plugin entry gets a note with the JSON to merge in. "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--quiet"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " drops the notes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "flags",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Flags"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeblock",
      "text": "  --format \u003cvalue\u003e\n        Output format: text or json (default text)\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every command also accepts "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--plain"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--project-dir \u003cvalue\u003e"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--quiet"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "; see "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help help"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
